  "summary": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Versions prior to 9.2.0077 have a heap-buffer-overflow and a…",
  "details": "Vim is an open source, command line text editor. Versions prior to 9.2.0077 have a heap-buffer-overflow and a segmentation fault (SEGV) exist in Vim's swap file recovery logic. Both are caused by unvalidated fields read from crafted pointer blocks within a swap file. Version 9.2.0077 fixes the issue.",
